WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.978
A target architecture
holds across hundreds

2
00:00:02.978 --> 00:00:05.675
of teams only if each
decision has an owner.

3
00:00:05.675 --> 00:00:08.882
No federal rule demands an
architecture review board,

4
00:00:08.882 --> 00:00:12.802
but several demand what one
produces: an enterprise architecture,

5
00:00:12.802 --> 00:00:16.437
and controlled change with
security and privacy at the table.

6
00:00:16.437 --> 00:00:19.000
The rule here is one decider per decision.

7
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.275
The chief architect decides
standards and designs.

8
00:00:22.275 --> 00:00:25.200
Application owners decide dispositions.

9
00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.934
The authorizing official
alone accepts risk,

10
00:00:27.934 --> 00:00:30.812
and observes the board
rather than sitting on it.

11
00:00:30.812 --> 00:00:35.150
And the CIO, not the board,
approves what the agency buys.

12
00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:38.625
So the CIO charters the
board and names its chair.

13
00:00:38.625 --> 00:00:39.910
Then come the gates.
